Ported from LizardByte/build-deps (MIT licence), commit d0ac5ef4b7673a8d8d2b03981ab5226cbf25810c:
https://github.com/LizardByte/build-deps/blob/d0ac5ef4b7673a8d8d2b03981ab5226cbf25810c/patches/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/cbs/02-remove-register.patch
Content unchanged. It applies cleanly to FFmpeg 9.0.2.

Why: Sunshine's cbs.cpp includes cbs_h264.h, which pulls in get_bits.h. Sunshine includes it from
C++23 code, where the `register` storage class is ill-formed, so it is removed.
The other two LizardByte cbs patches are not needed: 01-explicit-intmath only matters for their
separately compiled subset of sources, while the full libavcodec build includes intmath.h anyway.

Register storage specifier is an error for modern compiler and generally ignored anyway.

diff --git a/libavcodec/get_bits.h b/libavcodec/get_bits.h
